Welcome to BusyLinux.

Alpine's userspace, a kernel built from tinyconfig for this machine, and
BusyBox init -- no OpenRC, no display manager. /etc/init.d/rcS starts whatever
services happen to be installed; a desktop session is started by hand.

  apk add <package>            about 36,000 packages in Alpine edge
  apk add <package>@testing    opt into the tagged testing repository
  logread                      the system log, kept in memory by syslogd

The kernel and the init layer come from this machine's own repository in
/var/lib/busylinux/repo, so do not run "apk upgrade --prune" without it.

You may change this message by editing /etc/motd.
